hadiths[37]{hadithnumber,text}:
"104","From Ibn 'Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked: Which of the nations is most beloved to Allah? He replied: ""The most pious of the pious."" (Musnad Ahmad: 2107)"
"105","We used to await the Prophet's (peace be upon him) arrival, and one day a man emerged, his head dripping with water, having performed ablution or a bath. He then performed prayer, and when he finished, people began to ask him, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is this hair on your head?"" He replied, ""Indeed, the religion of Allah is ease."""""
"106","I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""There will be no house on the surface of the earth, whether in the east or in the west, that does not enter Islam, either by force or by choice. Allah will either honor them with honor or humble them with humility, and they will be content with that."""""
"107","I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""This matter will reach its peak, just as the day and night reach their peak. Allah will not leave a house in the east or the west without entering it with Islam, either with honor or with humiliation. Allah will honor Islam or humble disbelief."" Tameem al-Dari said: ""I have recognized this in my family. Indeed, good and noble qualities have been bestowed upon every Muslim from them, and indeed, humiliation, shame, and punishment have been bestowed upon every disbeliever from them."""""
"108","God will bless and exalt this religion through a people who have no nobility."
"109","From Abu Hurairah, who reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, Allah will strengthen this religion with the wicked man."""""
"110","An as was narrated by Anas bin Malik: A man would come to the Prophet, peace be upon him, seeking something from the world, and he would not leave until he made Islam more beloved to him and more exalted in his eyes than all that the world had to offer."
"111","And from him (it is narrated) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would not be asked about anything related to Islam except that he would give (an answer). A man came to him and asked, ""Give me a lot of something between two mountains from the charity."" He (the Prophet) returned to his people and said, ""O people! Islamize yourselves, for Muhammad gives what he is given, and he fears the Day of Reckoning."""""
"112","And from him, a great deal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to a man: ""Accept Islam."" The man said, ""Find me a guarantee."" He said, ""Accept Islam, even if you have a guarantee."" (Musnad Ahmad: 12084)"
"113","From Nasr bin Asim, from one of them, that he came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he had not been praying except for two rak'ats, so he accepted that from him."
"114","From Tameem ad-Dari, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! What is the Sunnah in a man from the People of the Book (and in a narration: from the People of Ignorance) who submits to the hand of a man from the Muslims? He said: ""He is the most superior of people in his life and his death."""""
"115","Abu Umama said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) when he was asked about the reward of the people of the Book and the polytheists. He said: ""Whoever among the people of the Book has believed, for him is his reward twice over, and for him is what is with us and upon him is what is upon us. And whoever among the polytheists has believed, for him is his reward, and for him is what is with us and upon him is what is upon us."""""
"116","Whoever has a mother, teaches her, and perfects her education, and perfects her upbringing, and sets her free, and then marries her, will have two rewards: the reward of a slave who fulfills the rights of Allah, and the reward of a man from the people of the Book who believes in what came to Jesus and what came to Muhammad, peace be upon him."
"117","When Allah favored me with Islam in my heart, I went to the Prophet (peace be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him. He stretched out his hand to me, and I said, ""I will not pledge allegiance to you until my past sins are forgiven."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""O Amr! Do you not know that the hijra is for the forgiveness of what has come before it, O Amr! Do you not know that Islam is for the forgiveness of what has come before it?"""""
"118","When 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, a man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! If I do good in Islam, will I be taken to account for my deeds in the Jahiliyya?"" He said, ""If you do good in Islam, you will not be taken to account for your deeds in the Jahiliyya. And if you do bad in Islam, you will be taken to account for the first and the last."""""
"119","I went out with my brother to visit the Messenger of Allah. We said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Our mother used to mend relationships, show hospitality to guests, and do good deeds, but what benefit did she gain from that in the Jahiliyya? He said: ""No."" We said: ""Then she used to give birth to a sister for us in the Jahiliyya, so what benefit did she gain from that?"" He said: ""The wailing and the moaning are in the Fire, except that the wailing is for the sake of Islam, and Allah will forgive her."""""
"120","I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, my father used to maintain family ties and perform good deeds, so is there any reward for him in this regard?"" He said: ""Indeed, your father sought a matter and it was granted to him."""""
"121","I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I have been in a state of ignorance, and I have been in a state of passion, and I have been in a state of mercy. Is there a reward for me in these?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""You have submitted to what you have submitted to, from good."""""
"122","A man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, a grey-haired old man who was leaning on a staff. He said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have committed many sins and wrongs, so will I be forgiven?"" He said, ""Are you not bearing witness that there is no god but Allah?"" He said, ""Yes, I am bearing witness and I testify that you are the Messenger of Allah."" He said, ""Your sins and wrongs have been forgiven."""""
"123","I have been commanded to fight the people until they say ""There is no god but Allah,"" and if they say it, then they will be spared their blood and property, except for what is rightfully theirs, and their reckoning will be with Allah alone. When the redness of the eyes appeared, 'Umar said to Abu Bakr, ""Will you fight them, and I have heard the Messenger of Allah say such and such."" He said, ""We will fight them, and Allah is our witness, I will not separate between prayer and charity, nor will I fight those who separate between them. We fought alongside him, and we saw that to be a guiding light."""""
"124","I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, ""There is no god but Allah,"" ""Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah,"" and they establish prayer and pay zakat. Then, their blood and property will be protected, and their reckoning will be with Allah alone."
"125","I was ordered to fight the people until they say: ""There is no god but Allah"" and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. If they say that and accept Islam, then accept our invitation to Islam, eat what we have slaughtered, and pray our prayer. Then their blood and property will be sacred, except for what is rightfully theirs. For them is what is for the Muslims and what is against them is what is against the Muslims."
"126","Abdullah narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, saying: I heard 'Uways (son of Abu 'Uways al-Thaqafi) saying: I visited the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) in Thaqif, and we were in a cave. As for those who were with me, except for myself and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), a man stood up and took him by the hand, saying: ""Let's go and kill him."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) called out: ""Is there not a witness that there is no god but Allah?"" He said: ""Yes, but he is only saying it as a means of seeking refuge."" Then he said: ""Return him."" (And in another narration: ""Let them go and kill him."") Then he said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say 'There is no god but Allah.' If they say it, then their blood and property will be inviolable, except for what is due to them. I told Shu'bah: ""Is there not a witness that there is no god but Allah, and that I am the Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""I think so, but I do not know."""""
"127","Whoever singles out Allah and disbelieves in what He has created from His attributes, Allah has cursed his wealth, his blood, and his reckoning."
"128","Ibn Mas'ud reported: Allah, the Exalted, has sent His Prophet to enter a man into Paradise, and he entered the Garden. When he was in it, he was a Jew, and when he was a Jew, he would read the Torah. Then they came to the Prophet's presence, and they were told to stop. In their midst was a sick man, and the Prophet asked, ""What is wrong with you?"" The sick man replied, ""We came to the presence of the Prophet and stopped."" Then the sick man recovered until he took the Torah, and then he came to the Prophet's presence and his community, and the Prophet said, ""This is your state and the state of your community. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and you are the Messenger of Allah."" Then he died, and the Prophet said to his companions, ""You will be resurrected."""""
"129","A man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah while he was sitting in a gathering. He asked permission to kill a man from the hypocrites, and the Messenger of Allah said: ""Is there not a witness that there is no god but Allah?"" The Ansari said, ""No, O Messenger of Allah, and there is no witness for him."" The Messenger of Allah said: ""Is there not a witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah?"" The Ansari said, ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Messenger of Allah said: ""Is he not praying?"" The Ansari said, ""No, O Messenger of Allah, and there is no prayer for him."" The Messenger of Allah said: ""Those are the ones whom Allah has abandoned from them."""""
"130","And from him, 'Abd al-Lah ibn 'Adi al-Ansari, who related that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was sitting when a man came to him, seeking permission to enter, and he remembered his meaning. (Musnad Ahmad: 24071)"
"131","Anas bin Malik reported that 'Itban had an eye problem, so he went to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and mentioned his problem. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said, ""Go to your house and pray in it until you are able to perform your prayer in it."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) stood up and those who were with him stood up with him. They would talk to each other and mention what they would encounter from the hypocrites. They would say, ""So-and-so is a hypocrite."" Anas said, ""We would report this to Malik bin Dukhshum, and he would say, 'Is it not that he bears witness that there is no god but Allah, and I am the Messenger of Allah?' And if he said, 'Yes, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I am the Messenger of Allah,' then the fire would not burn him, or he would not enter the fire.'"""""
"132","From Miqdad bin Aswad, may God have mercy on him, who said: ""O Messenger of Allah! If I were to meet a man from the infidels and he were to fight me, and we were to exchange blows, and he were to cut off my hand with a sword, and then he were to flee from me to a thorny tree, and he were to say, 'I have submitted to Allah, I will fight for Him, O Messenger of Allah?' (and in another narration: 'I will kill him, I will spare him, after he says that') then the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Do not kill him, for if you were to kill him, it would be before he says the word that he says, and you would be in his place before he says it, and he would be in your place before he says it."""""
"133","By the One Who is with me, no one from this Ummah, whether Jew or Christian, will hear of me and not believe in the one I was sent with, except that he will be from the companions of the Fire."
"134","From Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: ""He will not enter Paradise"" except that he is from the companions of the Fire."
"135","If ten men were to follow me, (the consequences) would be boundless, and if seventy men were to follow me, the entire Jewish community would have followed me with their faces turned towards the direction of the earth."
"136","My grandmother told me that my grandfather said: My mother told me that she heard my father say: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: There is no prayer for one who does not purify himself, and there is no purification for one who does not remember Allah, and there is no faith for one who does not believe in Allah, and there is no faith for one who does not love the Ansar."
"137","I said to 'Abi Muhyi'z: ""I said to 'Abi Jum'a, a man from the Companions, 'Tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him.' He said: 'Indeed, I will tell you a good hadith. We will accompany the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and Abu 'Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah with us. So I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Is there anyone better than us? We have accepted Islam with you and fought with you."" He said: ""Indeed, a people will come after you who will believe in me, though they will not see me.""'"""""
"138","Anas ibn Malik reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""I wish I had met my companions."" The companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""We are your companions."" He said: ""You are my companions, but my brothers are those who believed in me without seeing me."""""
"139","The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Good for one who has seen me and believed in me, and good for one who believes in me without having seen me, seven times."""""
"140","The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Good for one who believes in me and sees me once, and good for one who believes in me and does not see me seven times."""""
